	(text "Cable pads 1 VIN / 2 GND / 3 SCL / 4 SDA = first four pins of the GY-530 in the same order.\nGPIO1 and XSHUT of the GY-530 are not used (XSHUT has a pull-up on the carrier).\nPads: 1.0 mm holes for AWG26/24 stranded wire; strain-relieve cables at the case.\nStart at 100 kHz, then 400 kHz; check rise time with the real cable length."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 214.13 209.605 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.45 1.45)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "08196871-588f-46fb-b53a-033f0b665930")
	)
	(text "Eight VL53L0X carrier boards (GY-530) on soldered cables, one per mux channel: CH0 front, CH1-CH3 right side (front / middle / rear), CH4-CH7 J12-J15.\nAll sensors keep address 0x29, XSHUT not used. MUX_RSTn driven by ESP32-S3 GPIO37 (10k pull-up keeps the mux enabled during boot). Sensor VIN = +5 V (carrier has its own regulator); bus pull-ups 2.2k to +3.3 V."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 20.32 33.945 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.45 1.45)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "0b27cf73-13b4-4640-99b9-e39170d9d6b1")
	)
	(text "I2C address 0x70 (A0-A2 = GND). Write one channel mask only:\nCH0=0x01, CH1=0x02, CH2=0x04, CH3=0x08, CH4..CH7 = 0x10..0x80.\nPower-on and after MUX_RSTn: all channels disabled.\nIMU ICM-42670-P stays on the main bus at 0x68."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 193.3 111.76 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.45 1.45)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "30213959-da68-447b-b0de-df3850145839")
	)
